        "filled_by": "still",
        "at": "2026-09-04T13:54:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "EVIDENCE",
      "narration_text": "Let's look at the pros first. The model is incredibly accurate on pure lab mixtures. When trained on simple mixtures of thiophenol and alkanethiol, the CNN hit 99 percent validation accuracy. The architecture works perfectly on clean data.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "STILL",
        "source": "media",
        "motion": "kenburns"
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 15,
      "actual_duration_s": 14.87,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "STILL",
        "src": "media/B02.png",
        "filled_by": "still",
        "at": "2026-09-04T13:54:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "PROBLEM",
      "narration_text": "But here are the cons. An algorithm trained solely on simple mixtures struggles with complexity. When they added SERS data for 63 real metabolites and applied necessary normalization to avoid overfitting, the accuracy dropped to 84 percent.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "STILL",
        "source": "media",
        "motion": "kenburns"
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 18,
      "actual_duration_s": 14.78,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "STILL",
        "src": "media/B03.png",
        "filled_by": "still",
        "at": "2026-09-04T13:54:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "ASK",
      "narration_text": "So what's the plan? We need organically produced blood datasets. Specifically, SERS data for healthy versus NAFLD blood samples. We can't optimize our way out of a data gap.",
